    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-24T01:42:14+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-24T01:42:14+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-23T16:12:14Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-23T16:12:14Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred over the Tasman Sea extends a ridge westwards over central and eastern SA and a low pressure trough extends from WA over western SA. This trough will be very slow-moving for the rest of this week and over the weekend and the ridge will move away to the east. A weakening cold front will slip across southern coasts late Thursday and early Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-24T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-25T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-23T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-24T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h before dawn then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 29 to 35.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 3:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-25T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-26T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-24T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-25T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west in the afternoon and evening. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-26T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-27T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-25T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-26T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west in the afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h turning east to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-27T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-28T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-26T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-27T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to southeasterly 20 to 25 km/h tending east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
